index c7d4401..2179fef 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -148,6 +148,18 @@ The Observer receives only a bounded summary and fixed isometric/front/right/top
 PNG views. Dimensions and view mappings in `reconstruction-brief.json` are
 written by the host, not accepted from the model.
 
+After both earlier stages are accepted, omit the diagnostic mode flags to feed
+the validated brief and four controlled views into the existing incremental
+draft and produce editable SCAD/OBJ:
+
+```bash
+bun run mesh-to-cad --mesh reference.stl -o outputs/reference-cad \
+  --prompt "reconstruct the visible mechanical object faithfully"
+```
+
+This first generation slice is open-loop: it does not compare, score, refine,
+or repair the generated geometry against the private reference.
+
 That is text-only, part-by-part, with no image API and no Blender in the draft
 loop, and it is what you get with no flags at all. It is the cheapest useful
 configuration, not the strongest one.
